# The approval.md release gate's own files (B-167 CLASS-DIFF, B-167N NEW-CALLS).
# expected.json declares each new call's outcome and carries Carter's acceptance
# on a limiting one; accepted_by is text an author can write, so the control is
# this review plus approval.md's pin of the same file (PIN_EXPECTED in its ci.yml).
# Effective only once the main ruleset requires code-owner review (Carter's hand).
/scripts/approval-class-diff/expected.json   @soycarts
/scripts/approval-class-diff/                @soycarts
/scripts/approval-class-diff.sh              @soycarts
/.github/workflows/test.yml                  @soycarts
/.github/CODEOWNERS                          @soycarts
# B-167N fold 1 N7 (review-b's refute): the gated-tool list the extractor reads, the
# release enforcement point (Tag release tags only on a green test.yml), the manifest
# the release rule reads (previous-release.sh, S3), and the gate's own tests.
/install/install_approval.ts                 @soycarts
/.github/workflows/tag-release.yml           @soycarts
/scripts/tag-release.ts                      @soycarts
/scripts/tests/approval-class-diff.test.ts   @soycarts
/release/RC-MANIFEST.md                      @soycarts
# B-167N fold 2 M-D1 (review-b's DELTA L18777; lead RULING L18781): every path that can
# run code, or choose the code that runs, in the class-diff job before or during the
# check. The root files bun and npm read (lifecycle scripts, the lockfile, preload and
# registry config, tsconfig paths, .env)...
/package.json                                @soycarts
/bun.lock                                    @soycarts
/bun.lockb                                   @soycarts
/bunfig.toml                                 @soycarts
/.npmrc                                      @soycarts
/tsconfig.json                               @soycarts
/jsconfig.json                               @soycarts
/.env                                        @soycarts
/.env.*                                      @soycarts
